            "review_title": "Review at Co Ba Vung Tau",
            "review_text": "Thi Hoan N\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam41 contributions\n0\nCo Ba Vung Tau Banh Khot, 40B Tran Cao Van, Ward 6, District 3 charges 5,000 VND for take away boxes - please rate them.\nMar 2025 • Friends\nYesterday we went to dinner at the Banh Khot Co Ba Vung Tau restaurant at 40B Tran Cao Van, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City. We had dinner with a salad for 290,000 VND and a few other snacks and drinks. Our total bill was 650,000 VND. When there was still foods left, we asked to take home and the restaurant charged us 5,000 VND for the box. This is the first time I have been charged for the box. I don't know if they did the right thing or wrong because our bill was 650,000 VND, not cheap but not expensive, but they were too much when they charged for the box. Even though the box was only worth 5,000 VND, I was more upset because I have never heard of anyone charging for the box in Vietnam. In addition, the box had 2 holes drilled into it. It is unclear what kind of box they used to sell it to us. If the box was new and intact, it would not have had 2 holes like that.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nshould not go there. their foods are more expensive compared to other restaurants nearby\nService\nWritten March 7, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
