            "review_text": "Jenny S\nDundee, United Kingdom146 contributions\n0\nA great find!\nMar 2016 • Friends\nMy friend were recommended this restaurant by our hotel, Hotel L'Odeon as somewhere serving good local food nearby. We enjoyed it so much we ended up eating here three times. There was a large selection on the menu, one of the reasons we had no trouble returning, and the staff were patient with us as we made our way through the pages. Two of the three times I had the Banh Xeo and my favourite was with pork and shrimp. As this was my first time eating this dish or even seeing it the staff were lovely and helpful in showing us how to eat it - not so obvious if you are not familiar with Vietnamese food! We ordered fresh coconut to drink and the staff offered to chop it in two after so we could eat the inside as a small but delicious dessert. There seems to be quite a lot of chains and non-Vietnamese restaurants in this area so it was lovely to find somewhere the locals were eating and to eat good Vietnamese food, which is a large part of coming to this country!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 8, 2016",
